WEBVTT

01:57.010 --> 02:02.020
<b>Episode 12</b>

01:57.010 --> 02:02.020
<b>The Villainess and I Are in Love</b>

02:03.100 --> 02:04.070
Rae!

02:04.770 --> 02:06.840
I misjudged you.

02:06.840 --> 02:08.520
What might you be talking about?

02:08.520 --> 02:11.490
Don't play dumb with me. 
I'm talking about Claire.

02:15.870 --> 02:17.740
She cried all day yesterday.

02:20.060 --> 02:22.690
Please look after Miss Claire now.

02:22.690 --> 02:25.460
She gets lonely very easily.

02:25.750 --> 02:27.230
This is your fault!

02:27.660 --> 02:30.880
I lost. You defeated me.

02:30.880 --> 02:34.800
And I quit my job as her maid. 
I have no reason to stay with her.

02:34.800 --> 02:37.020
You'd give up just because of that?

02:37.020 --> 02:39.310
Is that all your feelings amount to?!

02:41.190 --> 02:43.270
Are you in any place to say that?

02:43.660 --> 02:47.440
You're the one who took Miss Claire from me!

02:47.440 --> 02:49.670
You're just running away!

02:49.670 --> 02:53.190
Even if I'd never shown up, 
you would've given up on her eventually!

02:53.190 --> 02:54.410
What grounds do you have to—

02:54.410 --> 02:56.420
"I don't care if it's unrequited."

02:56.420 --> 02:58.690
"As long as Claire's happy, that's enough."

02:58.690 --> 03:01.020
It's because you keep putting up 
that noble front!

03:01.330 --> 03:03.970
You're afraid of getting hurt.

03:03.970 --> 03:07.200
You don't want to feel the despair 
of not having your feelings returned.

03:07.200 --> 03:09.470
So you give up right from the beginning.

03:09.470 --> 03:11.340
You keep an escape route open at all times.

03:11.340 --> 03:12.290
You're wrong!

03:12.290 --> 03:14.620
<i>No, she's right.</i>

03:14.620 --> 03:17.340
<i>I don't care if it's unrequited? Really?</i>

03:17.340 --> 03:21.120
<i>No. I... I...</i>

03:21.500 --> 03:22.600
<i>The truth is...</i>

03:23.530 --> 03:26.320
<i>I want her to care. I want her to love me.</i>

03:26.320 --> 03:30.820
<i>I want her to fall in love with me 
the way I'm in love with her.</i>

03:31.300 --> 03:32.360
<i>But...</i>

03:32.360 --> 03:35.400
Some wishes can never be granted, 
no matter how much you want it!

03:35.400 --> 03:38.150
Miss Claire is a girl, and so am I!

03:38.150 --> 03:40.120
And she has someone else she likes!

03:40.120 --> 03:41.840
So you give up?

03:41.840 --> 03:44.870
You're happy with keeping up a superficial 
relationship and not even trying?

03:44.870 --> 03:46.520
That's enough for me!

03:46.520 --> 03:50.250
I'll stifle these feelings if that's 
what's best for Miss Claire!

03:51.920 --> 03:55.460
It won't work. A relationship like that 
will just fall apart one day.

03:59.550 --> 04:01.460
How do I know, you ask?

04:01.910 --> 04:03.840
Because it happened to me.

04:04.470 --> 04:08.850
I had someone I loved with 
all my heart, just like you do.

04:09.530 --> 04:12.120
I told myself I was fine 
as long as she was happy,

04:12.120 --> 04:14.610
even if she didn't end up with me.

04:14.610 --> 04:18.900
I just smashed my own feelings 
down harder and harder until...

04:19.490 --> 04:22.160
I made a terrible mistake.

04:22.710 --> 04:24.470
Considering the difference in our statuses,

04:24.470 --> 04:26.750
there was no way she 
would've turned me down.

04:27.230 --> 04:28.580
But still I...

04:30.240 --> 04:33.920
After a while, she vanished from the palace.

04:34.680 --> 04:38.040
Feelings that seek nothing in return 
will always become warped.

04:38.040 --> 04:42.180
The human heart is neither 
that strong nor that pure.

04:42.670 --> 04:46.650
After that, I started hanging 
around brothels in disguise.

04:47.160 --> 04:49.930
I figured relationships that were 
just about money and sex

04:49.930 --> 04:53.190
wouldn't hurt anyone, including myself.

04:53.650 --> 04:57.190
But I never felt fulfilled.

04:57.190 --> 05:02.770
I regret that I hurt her 
and lost her... even now.

05:03.910 --> 05:06.200
So what do you expect me to do?

05:07.110 --> 05:10.000
If you insist that you're giving up on Claire,

05:10.420 --> 05:13.080
I'll use her for my own amusement.

05:14.020 --> 05:17.710
Wh-What are you... Are you being serious?!

05:18.210 --> 05:21.090
I'll get all the enjoyment I want out of her.

05:21.090 --> 05:22.470
I won't let you do that!

05:22.470 --> 05:24.600
Oh? And how will you stop me?

05:29.410 --> 05:32.040
I'll challenge you at the Amour Ceremony!

05:32.040 --> 05:36.930
Offering your feelings on the Scales of Love 
to measure their depth, eh?

05:37.240 --> 05:38.660
Not a bad idea.

05:38.660 --> 05:41.220
But I've already beaten you once.

05:41.220 --> 05:44.110
I won't accept this challenge 
if there's nothing in it for me.

05:44.110 --> 05:47.410
If I win, you'll be mine, too.

05:47.410 --> 05:48.720
That's my condition.

05:48.720 --> 05:51.120
That's fine. I won't lose.

05:52.920 --> 05:54.380
Big words there!

05:55.480 --> 05:56.890
I like that look in your eyes.

06:01.300 --> 06:05.570
<i>She's the one person I can 
never give Miss Claire to.</i>

06:15.400 --> 06:18.650
A challenge? At the Amour Ceremony?

06:18.650 --> 06:19.540
Yeah.

06:20.260 --> 06:22.430
Giving me no say in it, again...

06:22.430 --> 06:23.830
What choice did we have?

06:23.830 --> 06:26.910
You refuse to tell us how you really feel.

06:29.740 --> 06:31.410
That's why we're fighting.

06:31.940 --> 06:36.290
Whose feelings will the Scales 
of Love really be weighing?

06:37.260 --> 06:42.110
Was it the two men whose 
feelings God tested, or...

06:52.120 --> 06:53.730
For crying out loud!

06:53.730 --> 06:55.730
It's simply too audacious!

06:55.730 --> 06:58.450
Just how little do they think 
of my own feelings?!

07:00.540 --> 07:02.170
Rae isn't here.

07:03.170 --> 07:05.390
She's been spending all her time working.

07:05.390 --> 07:07.200
Huh? Working?

07:07.520 --> 07:11.450
Remember all the monster-hunting quests 
posted on the Academy Knights' bulletin board?

07:12.020 --> 07:15.700
At a time like this? What is she thinking?

07:17.920 --> 07:19.330
Icicle Rain!

07:24.620 --> 07:26.740
Another magic stone...

07:26.740 --> 07:29.380
Ugh, nothing's dropping it!

07:30.300 --> 07:34.330
Well, the drop rate is 0.5%, after all...

07:34.870 --> 07:37.900
<i>But I don't have time 
to sit around complaining.</i>

07:38.400 --> 07:41.330
<i>Princess Manaria's definitely 
capable of finding the best offering</i>

07:41.330 --> 07:44.400
<i>that's considered next 
to impossible to obtain.</i>

07:45.460 --> 07:47.650
<i>This is my only chance at winning!</i>

07:47.650 --> 07:49.110
On to the next one!

08:14.350 --> 08:17.750
<i>I always said I wouldn't use my knowledge 
of the game to my advantage in love.</i>

08:17.750 --> 08:20.650
<i>That was the rule I set for myself.</i>

08:23.260 --> 08:27.860
<i>I thought it was cowardly to use things 
I only knew thanks to the unique circumstances</i>

08:27.860 --> 08:29.780
<i>of my reincarnation in that way.</i>

08:29.780 --> 08:32.860
<i>But that was just a noble front 
I was putting up.</i>

08:32.860 --> 08:35.760
<i>If I really want to end up with Miss Claire—</i>

08:35.760 --> 08:38.290
<i>if there's a future I want to attain, 
no matter what—</i>

08:41.750 --> 08:43.930
<i>I can't worry about how it looks to others!</i>

08:44.360 --> 08:46.740
Shoot... I'm running out of time.

08:48.180 --> 08:51.390
Don't worry. There's no way I'm giving up.

08:57.770 --> 08:58.730
Ralaire!

09:01.120 --> 09:02.470
Icicle Rai—

09:10.200 --> 09:11.860
Stone Cannon!

09:17.450 --> 09:20.480
If love was that easy to give up on,

09:20.480 --> 09:21.710
no one would suffer.

09:27.060 --> 09:30.680
What choice do I have? 
I love her, after all.

09:36.610 --> 09:39.320
<i>Wait for me, Miss Claire!</i>

09:54.890 --> 09:58.120
This year's Amour Ceremony seems 
to be another great success.

09:58.120 --> 10:02.880
Who are you hoping will win, Miss Claire? 
Rae or Princess Manaria?

10:03.250 --> 10:05.200
It doesn't even matter.

10:05.200 --> 10:08.920
People who treat me like a mere prize 
mean nothing to me.

10:08.920 --> 10:12.040
I'm hoping Rae will win.

10:12.040 --> 10:14.750
You're taking your friend's side, then?

10:14.750 --> 10:16.550
That's part of it, but...

10:16.870 --> 10:19.890
How do you feel about Rae, Miss Claire?

10:20.630 --> 10:21.810
What do you...

10:21.810 --> 10:24.150
Please tell me the truth.

10:25.420 --> 10:27.620
There's nothing to tell.

10:27.620 --> 10:29.270
That commoner is just...

10:30.030 --> 10:33.280
She's done nothing but spout nonsense 
since the moment we met.

10:33.280 --> 10:36.370
She even won my father's favor 
and became my maid.

10:36.780 --> 10:40.340
She'd always tease me with 
the crazy things she said and did...

10:40.340 --> 10:42.040
She was absolutely incorrigible.

10:42.040 --> 10:45.970
Honestly... That girl is just...

10:48.050 --> 10:51.340
far too cheeky for a commoner.

10:52.490 --> 10:55.930
I'm glad to see you're finally smiling.

10:55.930 --> 10:56.930
Huh?

10:57.870 --> 11:00.990
Miss Claire, if Rae does win,

11:00.990 --> 11:03.810
would you accept her as your maid again?

11:05.640 --> 11:08.970
I... can't do that.

11:10.180 --> 11:11.970
I am nobility.

11:11.970 --> 11:15.670
I could never bow to a commoner 
and beg her to be my maid.

11:15.670 --> 11:17.930
Not under any circumstances.

11:18.800 --> 11:20.350
I see.

11:20.350 --> 11:23.460
I guess being nobility 
is quite troublesome in itself.

11:24.440 --> 11:27.870
<i>Then I suppose I'll have 
to hope for a miracle.</i>

11:28.190 --> 11:29.410
<i>A miracle?</i>

11:29.410 --> 11:30.210
<i>Yes.</i>

11:30.700 --> 11:32.880
<i>A miracle that makes everything work out,</i>

11:32.880 --> 11:35.570
<i>like the kind that happens in stories.</i>

11:41.050 --> 11:42.510
Sister...

11:44.180 --> 11:45.910
Hi, Claire.

11:46.520 --> 11:47.150
Is that...

11:47.150 --> 11:48.540
She really found one?

11:48.540 --> 11:49.310
Wow...

11:49.840 --> 11:51.410
Is that flower...

11:51.410 --> 11:54.170
Yep. It's a Flower of Flora.

11:54.750 --> 11:55.570
Where's Rae?

11:59.280 --> 12:03.020
I see. Looks like I win again, huh?

12:05.560 --> 12:09.150
The scales of God have shown 
the truth in my heart.

12:09.510 --> 12:14.220
I swear to you, here and now, 
that I will protect you always.

12:15.800 --> 12:18.120
<i>The same thing she said back then...</i>

12:35.730 --> 12:37.110
Wait just a minute!

12:46.160 --> 12:47.330
Rae!

12:47.330 --> 12:50.330
H-How in the world 
did you end up in such a state?

13:05.030 --> 13:06.310
Huh...

13:06.310 --> 13:08.680
I guess you didn't run away after all.

13:08.680 --> 13:12.690
Why would I run away?! 
I told you I wouldn't lose!

13:13.690 --> 13:16.500
Miss Claire, please don't worry.

13:16.500 --> 13:18.510
I won't let her have you.

13:23.520 --> 13:27.170
I'm sorry to tell you this, 
but the contest is over.

13:27.170 --> 13:29.830
My offering is a Flower of Flora.

13:29.830 --> 13:31.930
Even in the long history of this ceremony,

13:31.930 --> 13:34.710
there's never been a greater offering. Right?

13:35.590 --> 13:37.710
My offering... is this.

13:40.190 --> 13:41.220
What?!

13:46.490 --> 13:47.970
What kind of joke is this?

13:48.770 --> 13:50.900
You'll see when I offer it.

13:51.480 --> 13:54.250
Very well, then. I'll go first.

13:55.520 --> 13:59.310
I offer the truth in my heart 
to God's judgment.

14:14.220 --> 14:17.250
Just look at that. 
There's no way she can win.

14:17.250 --> 14:19.800
What was Rae even thinking?

14:22.130 --> 14:23.430
My offering.

14:33.140 --> 14:35.080
That's nowhere near good enough!

14:35.080 --> 14:36.400
She's done for!

14:41.210 --> 14:43.230
You won't have faith in Rae?

14:51.240 --> 14:53.140
Looks like I win after—

15:09.500 --> 15:10.860
The scales...

15:16.070 --> 15:18.310
The Flower of Flora lost...

15:18.310 --> 15:22.570
This can't... Just what <i>was</i> that twig?

15:22.570 --> 15:25.070
It's called the Branch of Eternal Love.

15:25.070 --> 15:28.770
<i>It's a rare drop item that you have a very 
low chance of getting from a monster</i>

15:28.770 --> 15:30.580
<i>called the Entwined Tree.</i>

15:30.580 --> 15:33.500
<i>If you offer it, you get to 
see an exclusive event CG.</i>

15:33.500 --> 15:35.580
<i>It's what they call a secret item.</i>

15:36.100 --> 15:39.860
The Flower of Flora isn't 
the weightiest offering you can give?

15:39.860 --> 15:44.920
Yes, it is the weightiest 
of all offerings known to date.

15:44.920 --> 15:45.840
But...

15:46.340 --> 15:49.840
This just means something did exist 
that could surpass it.

15:52.220 --> 15:54.220
I told you, Manaria!

15:54.220 --> 15:57.140
She's not someone you can 
just handle in the normal way.

15:57.140 --> 15:58.100
Miss Claire.

15:59.820 --> 16:03.730
I'm not capable of the kind 
of love you see in stories.

16:03.730 --> 16:06.530
I can't even say what really matters 
without turning it into a joke.

16:06.870 --> 16:08.070
But...

16:08.760 --> 16:12.880
Regardless of whether the Scales of Love—
and God—acknowledge me,

16:12.880 --> 16:15.070
I still love you.

16:15.380 --> 16:18.560
No matter who I lose to, 
or who I have to kneel to,

16:18.560 --> 16:22.210
I will continue to love you all my life.

16:22.770 --> 16:23.960
So...

16:24.560 --> 16:29.320
Would you accept me, not as 
your maid but as your partner?

16:32.160 --> 16:34.060
I can't believe you.

16:36.850 --> 16:39.470
Well, I've lost this one!

16:39.470 --> 16:42.550
Rae, you really are just the best!

16:44.470 --> 16:48.700
S-Sister? What in the world is this about?

16:48.700 --> 16:50.360
Sorry, Claire.

16:50.360 --> 16:53.170
Rae is the one I've been after 
from the start!

16:53.170 --> 16:53.990
Huh?!

16:53.990 --> 16:57.750
So the reason you kept messing 
with Miss Claire was...

16:57.750 --> 17:01.670
I mean, your reactions 
were just so adorable.

17:01.670 --> 17:02.500
Tee-hee.

17:04.050 --> 17:06.380
Don't you "tee-hee" me!

17:06.380 --> 17:07.620
Let go of me!

17:07.620 --> 17:11.090
Oh, yes! You're even more adorable 
when you're resisting me!

17:12.590 --> 17:15.230
I love you like this.

17:15.230 --> 17:16.720
No!

17:18.480 --> 17:22.150
Rae belongs to me! 
You can't take my things from me!

17:28.650 --> 17:30.790
M-Miss Claire?

17:31.200 --> 17:34.030
W-Wait, no! I didn't mean it like—

17:34.030 --> 17:36.310
Miss Claire!

17:36.310 --> 17:39.540
G-Get off of me! We're in public!

17:39.540 --> 17:42.340
Nope! I love you, Miss Claire!

17:42.340 --> 17:44.540
Well, I hate you!

17:44.540 --> 17:46.880
So <i>get off of me</i>!

17:46.880 --> 17:49.920
You said I belong to you!

17:50.800 --> 17:54.740
Sh-Sh-Sh-Shut up! 
Don't say that! Forget about it!

17:51.380 --> 17:54.740
What are we being made to watch, exactly?

17:54.740 --> 17:56.760
Right now! That's an order!

17:56.760 --> 17:59.030
I'll never forget it! Not even in death!

17:57.440 --> 18:01.950
Princess Manaria, forgive me, 
but I believe this contest is decided.

17:59.780 --> 18:03.060
Miss Claire!

18:04.060 --> 18:05.610
Hey! Let go!

18:04.060 --> 18:05.610
It seems so.

18:06.690 --> 18:08.880
Get off of me!

18:08.880 --> 18:11.060
Nope!

19:46.550 --> 19:50.000
Sister... You're returning to Sousse?

19:50.000 --> 19:53.440
Yeah. The first prince died suddenly.

19:53.440 --> 19:55.780
Now the right of succession's been moved up,

19:55.780 --> 19:59.380
and I have to go right back into 
the same old messy family feud.

19:59.760 --> 20:01.920
Rae shot me down anyway,

20:01.920 --> 20:04.460
so I might as well go win the throne.

20:04.460 --> 20:07.310
Once that's over, 
I'll come bother you again.

20:07.310 --> 20:08.530
No need for that.

20:08.530 --> 20:10.690
Rae, you're being rude.

20:12.110 --> 20:14.440
My time here has been fun.

20:14.440 --> 20:15.620
For me, as well.

20:15.620 --> 20:16.440
Just go now.

20:16.440 --> 20:17.150
Rae!

20:17.460 --> 20:20.040
That hurt, Miss Claire! I love you!

20:20.040 --> 20:24.490
Really... You need to have 
more respect for royalty.

20:24.490 --> 20:29.060
I'm sorry, but my heart 
is already full of love for you!

20:29.570 --> 20:30.590
Urgh...

20:33.040 --> 20:36.470
Man, you two are so close now.

20:36.470 --> 20:38.550
Maybe I went too far.

20:41.110 --> 20:44.810
<i>Now that I think about it, maybe 
that was her goal from the start?</i>

20:44.810 --> 20:50.550
<i>To be the bad guy who'd push 
Miss Claire and me to get closer...</i>

20:50.550 --> 20:55.130
<i>Wait, even if that's true, 
there must have been a better way!</i>

20:55.130 --> 20:58.390
Claire, can I borrow Rae one last time?

21:01.070 --> 21:02.160
Bye!

21:06.220 --> 21:08.330
She came and went like the wind, huh?

21:10.130 --> 21:12.610
Now, allow me to officially say...

21:12.610 --> 21:14.710
Congratulations, Miss Claire.

21:14.710 --> 21:15.460
Huh?

21:15.460 --> 21:17.960
As long as Miss Claire is happy, I...

21:17.960 --> 21:20.780
Don't cry, Loretta! You've still got me!

21:20.780 --> 21:22.770
Love takes a different form for everyone.

21:22.770 --> 21:24.700
We'll be rooting for you.

21:24.700 --> 21:26.910
W-Wait just a moment!

21:26.910 --> 21:28.990
What are you all talking about?

21:28.990 --> 21:30.350
What else?

21:30.670 --> 21:32.630
You're gonna be Rae's bride, aren't you?

21:32.630 --> 21:33.730
Aren't you?

21:32.630 --> 21:33.730
Right?

21:32.630 --> 21:33.730
Yes?

21:32.630 --> 21:33.730
Are you not?

21:33.730 --> 21:35.340
B-Bride?

21:35.340 --> 21:38.440
Me, Claire François? A commoner's bride?

21:38.440 --> 21:41.120
Rae's the one who'll be the bride.

21:41.120 --> 21:41.950
Wait!

21:41.950 --> 21:43.700
I didn't mean that!

21:46.590 --> 21:49.520
<i>Rae, I want to ask you something.</i>

21:51.280 --> 21:52.830
What is it?

21:53.930 --> 21:55.540
Just who are you?

21:57.730 --> 22:00.590
You knew of an unknown offering 
that surpassed the Flower of Flora,

22:00.900 --> 22:04.870
and I heard you neutralized an unknown 
poison from the Nur Empire, too.

22:05.490 --> 22:07.610
Where did you get that knowledge?

22:07.610 --> 22:08.810
I can't answer that.

22:09.080 --> 22:11.060
Are you a spy from the Empire?

22:11.060 --> 22:12.290
No.

22:12.290 --> 22:13.440
Really?

22:13.440 --> 22:15.090
I swear to Miss Claire.

22:19.050 --> 22:22.570
<i>Yes. It's all for Miss Claire...</i>

22:33.210 --> 22:36.910
<i>and to stop the tragedy 
that awaits in the future.</i>

22:43.220 --> 22:45.950
You swear to Miss Claire, huh?

22:47.470 --> 22:51.100
I believe that more than 
I'd believe you swearing to any god.

22:51.840 --> 22:54.130
Take care of Claire, all right?

22:54.130 --> 22:55.510
No need to ask.

23:04.110 --> 23:07.990
Miss Claire! Say that one thing again!

23:08.330 --> 23:09.740
What are you talking about?

23:09.740 --> 23:12.570
Look at you, pretending you don't know! 
You're just the cutest!

23:12.570 --> 23:14.750
Don't get ahead of yourself.

23:14.750 --> 23:16.370
Listen, Rae, you're not even...

23:16.910 --> 23:18.370
Not even what?

23:22.940 --> 23:26.030
I notice you're calling me by my name.

23:26.550 --> 23:28.390
I don't know what you mean.

23:29.450 --> 23:32.140
Miss Claire, I truly love you.

23:33.380 --> 23:35.150
I can't hear you.

23:37.650 --> 23:40.900
I love you, Miss Claire!

23:43.320 --> 23:45.350
Hey! Not in front of people! 
Have you no shame?!

23:43.320 --> 23:46.520
Miss Claire! Miss Claire! Miss Claire!

23:45.350 --> 23:47.910
Let go of me! What are you—

23:47.910 --> 23:50.860
I love you! I always have!

23:49.260 --> 23:51.910
Okay, I get it! Quiet down!

23:51.910 --> 23:53.910
And I always will!

